/**
 * @defgroup Con2Prim Con2Prim Gem
 *
 * @brief The @gc2p gem provides conservative-to-primitive variable solvers,
 *        auxiliary functions, a primitive-to-conservative function, etc.
 *
 * There is no (known) closed-form solution that allows for directly computing
 * the primitive variables from the conservative variables, so this inversion
 * must be done numerically using an iterative solver. This gem also provides some
 * other auxiliary functions, such as computing the conservatives and
 * stress-energy tensor from the primitive variables.
 *
 * The solvers are split by the types of EOS they support, which are detailed
 * more explicitly within the documentation subpages.
 *
 * @section c2p_calling_contract Recovery calling contract
 *
 * Every solver, selector, and multi-method recovery driver takes undensitized
 * conservatives: D = rho W, tau, and S_i. Use ghl_undensitize_conservatives()
 * on densitized evolution variables before recovery. In contrast,
 * ghl_apply_conservative_limits() operates on densitized conservatives, and
 * ghl_compute_conservs() / ghl_compute_conservs_and_Tmunu() produce them.
 *
 * Initialize the EOS and its function-pointer dispatch, metric and ADM
 * auxiliaries, and ghl_con2prim_diagnostics before recovery. The primitive
 * argument supplies the magnetic field and any method-specific initial guess;
 * it receives the recovered state on success and may be modified on failure.
 * With primitive guessing disabled or a direct solver call, the caller supplies
 * the required guess. In particular, tabulated Palenzuela uses incoming Y_e and
 * temperature, bounding composition rather than reconstructing it from the
 * conservatives. Its fixed-temperature mode uses the supplied temperature,
 * subject to EOS bounds and an internal retry that can reset it to T_min.
 *
 * Recovery returns ghl_success or a numerical/EOS error. An unsupported method
 * selection returns ghl_error_invalid_c2p_key; tabulated selection without
 * HDF5 returns ghl_error_used_disabled_hdf5. Multi-method drivers try configured
 * backups after recoverable errors. Apply
 * ghl_enforce_primitive_limits_and_compute_u0() afterward when configured
 * primitive bounds are required, then recompute conservatives for consistency.
 *
 * @section c2p_solver_settings Iteration controls
 *
 * ghl_parameters::con2prim_max_iterations and
 * ghl_parameters::con2prim_solver_tolerance control Noble Newton solves.
 * Each Newton invocation has its own iteration budget. Convergence requires
 * both the Newton correction (relative to the updated variable, or absolute
 * when it is zero) and the recomputed residual objective to satisfy the
 * tolerance. Hybrid Noble2D measures its bounded squared-velocity coordinate
 * using the update actually applied after validation. Other coordinates and
 * tabulated recovery retain the proposed correction, because validation can
 * hide a large step even when the absolute residual is small.
 * Font, Palenzuela, and Newman use local iteration and tolerance settings;
 * changing those public Noble controls does not tune these methods.
 * Font limits its outer iterations and detects exact cycles in each inner
 * density solve, allowing slowly converging inner solves to continue beyond
 * the outer iteration budget. Only a completed inner solve supplies a new
 * density seed for a retry. Within a common EOS-clamped density branch,
 * geometric damping, applied only where it contracts faster than the undamped
 * map, suppresses nearly reciprocal oscillations while the undamped density
 * residual still determines convergence.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup hyb_c2p Hybrid EOS Con2Prim
 * @ingroup Con2Prim
 *
 * The routines provided for the hybrid (a.k.a. piecewise polytrope)
 * equation of state are given in the table below.
 *
 * | Method                    | Function Name                   | Reference |
 * |:-------------------------:|:-------------------------------:|:------------:|
 * | Noble2D                   | @ref ghl_hybrid_Noble2D              | [Noble _et al._ (2006)](https://arxiv.org/abs/astro-ph/0512420) |
 * | Noble1D                   | @ref ghl_hybrid_Noble1D              | [Noble _et al._ (2006)](https://arxiv.org/abs/astro-ph/0512420) |
 * | Noble1D with entropy      | @ref ghl_hybrid_Noble1D_entropy      | [Noble _et al._ (2006)](https://arxiv.org/abs/astro-ph/0512420); entropy definition from [Noble _et al._ (2009)](https://arxiv.org/abs/0808.3140) |
 * | Noble1D entropy-rho       | @ref ghl_hybrid_Noble1D_entropy2     | [Noble _et al._ (2006)](https://arxiv.org/abs/astro-ph/0512420); density solve for one-piece EOS with \f$\Gamma_{\rm th}=\Gamma_{\rm ppoly}\f$ |
 * | Font1D                    | @ref ghl_hybrid_Font1D               | [Font _et al._ (2000)](https://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/9811015) |
 * | Palenzuela1D              | @ref ghl_hybrid_Palenzuela1D_energy  | [Palenzuela _et al._ (2015)](https://arxiv.org/abs/1505.01607) |
 * | Palenzuela1D with entropy | @ref ghl_hybrid_Palenzuela1D_entropy | [Werneck _et al._ (2023)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.14487) |
 *
 * The simple EOS can also use all these methods **except** for Font1D which
 * assumes that there's a split between cold and thermal parts. Both Noble
 * entropy methods require neos == 1 and Gamma_th == Gamma_ppoly[0]; hybrid
 * metadata must describe the same one-piece constant-Gamma law as the simple EOS.
 *
 * Ordinary hybrid Noble finalization keeps a speed-limited state consistent
 * with the solved variable by recomputing \f$\rho=D/W_{\rm final}\f$ and the
 * enthalpy density \f$w=Z/W_{\rm final}^2\f$, preserving
 * \f$Z=\rho h W_{\rm final}^2\f$. Near the cold-pressure boundary, a
 * roundoff-sized change in \f$w\f$ can be amplified when pressure is recovered
 * by subtraction. The resulting pressure sign is toolchain-sensitive and the
 * consistent closure can expose more `ghl_error_neg_pressure` cases than the
 * former mixed-state closure. Configure a robust later backup, such as Font1D,
 * when these marginal states must recover.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup tab_c2p Tabulated EOS Con2Prim
 * @ingroup Con2Prim
 *
 * The routines provided for the tabulated equation of state are given in the table below.
 *
 * | Method                    | Function Name                           | Reference |
 * |:-------------------------:|:---------------------------------------:|:------------:|
 * | Noble2D                   | @ref ghl_tabulated_Noble2D              | [Noble _et al._ (2006)](https://arxiv.org/abs/astro-ph/0512420) |
 * | Newman1D                  | @ref ghl_tabulated_Newman1D_energy      | [Newman & Hamlin (2014)](https://epubs.siam.org/doi/10.1137/140956749) |
 * | Newman1D with entropy     | @ref ghl_tabulated_Newman1D_entropy     | [Werneck _et al._ (2023)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.14487) |
 * | Palenzuela1D              | @ref ghl_tabulated_Palenzuela1D_energy  | [Palenzuela _et al._ (2015)](https://arxiv.org/abs/1505.01607) |
 * | Palenzuela1D with entropy | @ref ghl_tabulated_Palenzuela1D_entropy | [Werneck _et al._ (2023)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.14487) |
 *
 * These solvers require tabulated EOS support. Their declarations remain
 * visible in public headers when GHL_DISABLE_HDF5 is defined, but the solver
 * implementations are excluded from that build.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup c2p_guess Primitive Initial Guesses
 * @ingroup Con2Prim
 *
 * These routines supply seeds for recovery; they do not establish convergence
 * or EOS admissibility. The NN predicts the Palenzuela variable x=hW from the
 * fixed input layout {q,r,s,t}; normal solvers still perform recovery.
 *
 * NN inference, validation, cleanup, and primitive-guess helpers are built
 * without HDF5. The model loaders remain callable in that mode and return
 * ghl_error_used_disabled_hdf5. Successful loading replaces the EOS-owned
 * model; failed loading preserves it. See ghl_c2p_nn_model for ownership.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup c2p_internal Internal Con2Prim Routines
 * @ingroup Con2Prim
 *
 * These are implementation helpers used by the @ref Con2Prim routines.
 * Private headers such as roots.h and utils_Palenzuela1D.h are not installed;
 * external linkage alone does not make their routines supported public APIs.
 * ghl_palenzuela_quantities remains declared for compatibility, while active
 * Palenzuela recovery uses private workspace types.
 */
